cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "VMI workflow: interactive velocity-map imaging coincidence analysis"
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Tao
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EXAMPLE/vmi-workflow"
keywords:
  - velocity-map imaging
  - VMI
  - photoelectron photoion coincidence
  - Abel inversion
  - rBasex
  - spectroscopy
abstract: "An interactive PySide6 workstation for velocity-map imaging (VMI) photoelectron/photoion coincidence analysis: trigger-based event pairing, ion time-of-flight selection, image-center estimation, denoised polar binning, and rBasex Abel inversion to recover radial speed and angular-anisotropy (beta) distributions."
